---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: seam-contracts-seam-birth-rule
purpose: >
  `elohim-seam-contracts` (lib `seam_contracts`) — the concern canon's compile-shape
  home: `Answer<T>` (C4), `ReasonLabel` (C8), and the `Arbitrated`/`Quiescent`/
  `Liveness` property harnesses (C2/C6b/C3). Unlike a per-seam crate
  (elohim-storage, doorway, steward/node), this leaf carries GENERIC vocabulary
  every consumer inherits — so a new shared type minted here has a wider blast
  radius than a per-seam instantiation, and the birth rule (plan task P4.5)
  applies with extra weight: answer the canon here, or the gap ships to every
  crate that depends on this one.
rules:
  - id: seam-birth-rule
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "*.rs"
      contains-any: ["pub enum ", "pub trait ", "Answer<", "Reason {", "Outcome {",
                     "Decision {", "Verdict {", "ViolationClass {"]
    dedupe-of: ".claude/skills/p2p-design-gate/SKILL.md (Step 4: Concern-Canon Answer) + elohim/sdk/schemas/v1/manifest/seam-registry.schema.json (the registry a new decision surface conforms to)"
    why: >
      A new pub enum/trait here (or a new `Answer<T>`/`ReasonLabel`-shaped type)
      is exactly what the seam-concern contract architecture's birth rule governs
      — with the added weight that this crate's vocabulary is GENERIC: a gap here
      isn't one seam's problem, it's inherited by every crate that depends on
      `seam_contracts`. Before shipping one: walk `p2p-design-gate` Step 4 —
      answer C0-C14 (`answered`/`partial`/`unbound`/`n-a`-with-justification)
      against the guarantee in its canon home (predicate-bearing classes are
      enforcement rows in `.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml`, currently C2/C6a; the
      rest are Precedent-shaped rows in `.claude/epr-meta/concerns.yaml`). Then
      register the point: a genuinely new CROSS-CUTTING shape (a fourth harness
      alongside Arbitrated/Quiescent/Liveness, a new wire-facing reason/state
      enum) gets its own `crates/seam-contracts/seam-registry.yaml` (schema:
      `elohim/sdk/schemas/v1/manifest/seam-registry.schema.json`; this crate has
      none yet — create it at that point); a per-seam INSTANTIATION of `Answer<T>`
      or a `ReasonLabel` impl registers in the CONSUMING crate's own
      `seam-registry.yaml` instead (elohim-storage, doorway/doorway-service,
      steward/node already have one). The census (`placement-audit.py
      --epr-meta`) is the enforcement backstop, not this advisory. This rule
      matches file CONTENT, not added lines, so an edit anywhere in
      `answer.rs`/`reason.rs`/`harness/*.rs` (already soaked in these tokens)
      re-fires too — the accepted cost of a declarative advisory that never
      blocks (never a validator: this is a judgement call, not a textual proof).
cites:
  - seam-concern-contract-architecture-plan
