# crates/seam-contracts — seam birth rule (concern canon)

`src/lib.rs`'s module doc describes the crate's own doc convention (every public
item names its concerns, forcing incident, and contract test — the `#![deny(missing_docs)]`
half of that is already structural). This manifest adds the other half — the
edit-time reminder that a *new* generic decision-surface shape (plan task P4.5)
must answer the concern canon and register before it ships, since what lands here
is inherited by every consumer, not scoped to one seam. See
`.claude/epr-meta/policies.yaml` + `.claude/epr-meta/concerns.yaml` for the sixteen
classes (C0-C14, C6 split C6a/C6b) and the `p2p-design-gate` skill's Step 4 for the
per-class checklist.
